I look in the mirror.
This new shirt is bigger than the previous one.
It fits me perfectly.
The shoulders are also not tight anymore.
This is much better for me than that size.
I smile and turn toward bhaiya.
"Bhaiya, this is exactly right," I say.
"I will take this shirt."
He smiles and says, "Okay, madam."
"Do I have to give any more money?" I ask.
"No madam, the price of both is the same," he replies.
I give the small shirt back to him.
"Thank you very much for exchanging it so easily, bhaiya," I say.
He puts the new shirt in a bag.
He gives the receipt and bag to me.
I take the bag and come out of the shop.
Outside, there is still humidity in the air.
But now I am fully prepared for the changing season.
Happily, I catch my bus to go home.
